<Project>

  <!--
    Impeller has no 32-bit story. LibreHardwareMonitor's kernel driver must match the bitness of
    the process that loads it, the engine service runs AnyCPU (so 64-bit on 64-bit Windows), and
    a 32-bit shell talking to a 64-bit service is a mismatch nobody would look for.

    This exists because the mismatch is silent by default. The WinUI template shipped
    <Platforms>x86;x64;ARM64</Platforms>, `dotnet sln add` pinned the solution to the first entry,
    and the only visible symptom was a "win-x86" segment in an output path. Failing the build
    turns that into something you cannot walk past.

    ARM64 is deliberately allowed; only x86 is rejected.
  -->
  <Target Name="ImpellerRejectX86"
          BeforeTargets="Build;Publish"
          Condition="'$(PlatformTarget)' == 'x86' Or '$(Platform)' == 'x86' Or '$(RuntimeIdentifier)' == 'win-x86'">
    <Error Code="IMP0001"
           Text="Impeller does not support 32-bit builds (Platform='$(Platform)', PlatformTarget='$(PlatformTarget)', RuntimeIdentifier='$(RuntimeIdentifier)'). Check for a stray &lt;Platform&gt; element in Impeller.slnx or a &lt;Platforms&gt; list in the project." />
  </Target>

</Project>
